      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ONE MORE REASON (6) was far too good in her qualifier, leading from a couple of spots wider than this before going on to score by close to 5m. That continued her consistent form at this circuit and distance, highlighted by her Group 1 placing in the Breeders Challenge final when only 5m off record-breaking filly Ark Sea. That looks very strong form for this. Victorian filly ROCKNROLL WILLOW (8) stretched her winning run to four when she proved too good at this circuit and distance first up. A wider draw makes this tougher but she is two from two when second-up so should be improved. FAKE FRIENDS (5) led from wider and stuck on for second to ROCKNROLL WILLOW in the heats. Draws inside that rival this time so can be prominent as can OSHLEY (4) who draws much better than when she raced three wide without cover to stuck on to place behind ONE MORE REASON last start. THE ATTRACTOR (2) has exotic claims from a low draw.",
